Duration about 0.9 s. No load error, no import error, no syntax error.

Failing tests and reasons:

1. `delta_staged_addition_validates` — reports "V2 baseline deltas must
   be empty". The validator lacks the v1-plus-staged-delta rule.
2. `delta_staged_removal_of_v1_survivor_validates` — same reason.
3. `delta_unexplained_baseline_rejected` — reports "database v2 baseline
   entries differ from v1" instead of "does not match v1 plus the staged
   delta". The v2-against-v1-plus-delta check is missing.
4. `preview_stages_current_delta_and_rebinds_four_files` — stages
   `additions=0`. The four-file shape holds; the current-delta staging is
   missing.
5. `cli_accepts_owner_and_rationale` — throws "Unsupported architecture
   reconciliation argument: --owner".
6. `cli_forwards_review_metadata_to_apply` — same, parse throws first.
7. `apply_allows_reviewed_candidate_write` — rejects with "Candidate v2
   reconciliation cannot write before acceptance".
8. `overlay_pins_snapshot_over_proposed_bytes` — finds
   `computeAnalyzerInputSnapshotWithOverlay` undefined.
9. `ci_runs_check_under_policy_v2_with_skip` — the boundary step runs
   `pnpm architecture:check --skip-input-snapshot-pin` with no
   `--policy v2`.

Passing guards: `route_fixture_positive_control`,
`delta_unstaged_addition_rejected`, `delta_malformed_record_rejected`.
The base shape check already rejects non-empty deltas and malformed
records, and the fixture manifest validates before any mutation.

## Guarded test edits from c6e3e4462 (for reviewer audit)

c6e3e4462 edits three existing test files. None of these edits was
copied into an existing file; the Red file only adds. Green must port
each edit with its production change.

1. `architecture-ci-input-pin.test.ts` — the workflow expectation gains
   `--policy v2`. Reason: the CI step runs the check under policy v2
   (220e5886d). The old expectation fails after Green.
2. `reconciliation-manifest-v2.red.test.ts` — the case is renamed to
   "staged baseline deltas"; the three `toEqual([])` assertions become
   non-empty array assertions. Reason: the committed manifest stages the
   reviewed delta instead of empty arrays.
3. `v2-baseline-delta.test.ts` — the addition and removal fixtures append
   to the committed staged delta instead of overwriting it; the removal
   case picks a v1 survivor still present in v2. Reason: fixtures must
   build on the committed staged delta once the manifest stages one.

